---
// Mission: approved 501(c)(3) copy. Reverent typography, generous breathing room.
---

<section id="mission" class="section">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Mission</p>
      <span class="rule mt-6"></span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal mt-10 font-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,5vw,4rem)] leading-[1.05] text-ink max-w-3xl">
      To uplift lives through the transformative power of music.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-x-12 gap-y-10">
      <div class="reveal md:col-span-7 space-y-6 text-ink/80 text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          St John Coltrane Arts, based in San Francisco, California, is a charitable
          organization dedicated to providing inclusive creative music education and
          cultural enrichment to underserved youth and young adults in San Francisco.
          Our commitment is to uplift lives through the transformative power of music
          guided by the artistic and spiritual work and legacy of the master American
          Jazz, St John Coltrane. We are a cross-cultural and cross-generational
          organization, and founders Archbishop Reverend King and Reverend Mother
          Marina King have been serving the San Francisco and SF Bay Area as a Global
          Spiritual Community for six decades with the song and word of
          &ldquo;A Love Supreme&rdquo; 1965.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our curriculum-based multi-disciplinary music program integrates music theory,
          performance, and the science of sound. The program fosters creativity,
          discipline, and community engagement, serving as a vehicle for personal growth
          and academic enrichment. Our team includes university-level instructors with
          professional musicians and educators mentoring students in individual and
          ensemble settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          The program develops musical talent and also provides a safe and nurturing
          environment supporting self-expression, collaboration, and purpose. Focusing
          on the art and science of music, we inspire participants to connect music with
          broader educational and career pathways. Rooted in musical training, our
          teaching extends beyond music to promote holistic development and access to
          opportunities that would otherwise be unavailable to our students.
        </p>
        <p>
          Through this dedicated work, Saint John Coltrane Arts fosters a new generation
          of artists, thinkers, and leaders carrying forward a musical and thought-provoking
          legacy of Saint John Coltrane &mdash; fostering a new generation of compassion,
          excellence, and empowered creative spirit.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="reveal md:col-span-4 md:col-start-9">
        <div class="border-l border-gold/40 pl-6 space-y-8">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow text-muted">Pillars</p>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 font-display text-2xl text-ink/90">
              <li>Theory</li>
              <li>Performance</li>
              <li>The Science of Sound</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow text-muted">Status</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-ink/80">
              501(c)(3) nonprofit. Secular, attached to the Saint John Coltrane Church.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
